@startuml Sum_Ssfm_Service0x14_Handler
top to bottom direction
skinparam linetype ortho

legend top left
    "Sum_Ssfm_Service0x14_Handler"

**Interfaces Legend**
    //ri107 //: ServiceRequestNotification
    //II152 //: ERRH_ExecutionStatus / SSM_ExecutionStatus
	//pi103 //: SerialData<n>_FcFA
	//pi106 //: SerialData<n>_FoFA
	//pi109 //: SerialData<n>_FpFA
	//pi112 //: SerialData<n>_FsFA
	//pi138 //: RunCrankInputStuckHigh_FA_StatusRequest
	//pi139 //: RunCrankInputStuckLow_FA_StatusRequest
	//II12  //: Signal<n>_LcFA
	//pi116 //: LIN_Signal<n>_LcFA
	//II13  //:  Signal<n>_Inv
	//pi118 //: SSFM_ClearDiagReq
	//II182 //: Service14requested
endlegend

note top of EC
It is responsible for handling the SSFM part of service 0x14. Hence, it updates all the interfaces according to the fact that all DTCs have been cleared. 
It communicates the occurrence of a confirmed service 0x14 to the SOH. 
end note

component [SSFM::Sum_Ssfm_Service0x14_Handler] as EC{
    portin ri107
    portout pi103
	portout pi106
	portout pi109
	portout pi112
	portout pi113
	portout pi114
	portout pi116
	portout pi118
    portout pi130
	
    [Sum_Ssfm_Service_0x14_Handler]  as E
}
    interface II152
	interface II12
	interface II13

    ri107 -> E
	II152 -> E
    E -> pi103
    E -> pi106
    E -> pi109
    E -> pi112
    E -> pi113
    E -> pi114
	E -> II12
    E -> pi116 
    E -> pi118
    E -> pi130
    E -> II13	


@enduml
